      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_3",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "ESET_Cyberattacks-Ukrainian-power-industry(01-20-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s1"
      },
      "text": "The attackers sent spearphishing emails to potential victims yesterday.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_6",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "ESET_Cyberattacks-Ukrainian-power-industry(01-20-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s4"
      },
      "text": "We have observed the same interesting technique used by the BlackEnergy group in the past.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_11",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "ESET_Cyberattacks-Ukrainian-power-industry(01-20-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s4"
      },
      "text": "Disassembled code from dropped executable The server hosting the final payload is located in Ukraine and was taken offline after a notification from CERT-UA and CyS-CERT.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_12",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "ESET_Cyberattacks-Ukrainian-power-industry(01-20-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s1"
      },
      "text": "We expected to see the BlackEnergy malware as the final payload, but a different malware was used this time.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_13",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "ESET_Cyberattacks-Ukrainian-power-industry(01-20-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s2"
      },
      "text": "The attackers used modified versions of an open-source gcat backdoor written in the Python programming language.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_15",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "ESET_Cyberattacks-Ukrainian-power-industry(01-20-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s4"
      },
      "text": "Obfuscated code of GCat backdoor This backdoor is able to download executables and execute shell-commands.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_16",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "ESET_Cyberattacks-Ukrainian-power-industry(01-20-2016)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 4,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p4_s5"
      },
      "text": "Other GCat backdoor functionality, such as making screenshots, keylogging, or uploading files, was removed from the source code.",
